  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CACI Federal obligated $2.8B in FY2026 to date. CACI Federal received 216 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $12.9M. Obligations are down 20.9% year over year. Historical obligations show a rise from $1.3B in FY21 to $3.5B in FY25, with FY26 returning to $2.8B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.5B, followed by the General Services Administration at $950M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market by NAICS, accounting for $1.1B of obligations, and Engineering Services is the second-largest market at $648M. Smaller but notable markets include Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $258M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $231M. Contract activity spans a mixture of IT, engineering, investigations, and R&D work. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year totals or award values for listed large or expiring contracts.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did CACI Federal's FY2026 obligations compare with prior years?",
        "body": "CACI Federal obligated $2.8B in FY2026 to date, compared with $3.5B in FY25 and $2.8B in FY24. Obligations increased from $1.3B in FY21 to $2.3B in FY23 before peaking at $3.5B in FY25. Obligations are down 20.9% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top federal buyers of CACI Federal in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B from CACI Federal, making it the largest buyer. The General Services Administration obligated $950M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $215M. NASA obligated $135M and the Department of the Interior obligated $26.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does CACI Federal make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "CACI Federal made $2.8B from federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. CACI Federal received 216 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $12.9M. Historical context shows obligations rose from $1.3B in FY21 to $3.5B in FY25 before landing at $2.8B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from CACI Federal?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $1.5B. The General Services Administration follows with $950M, the Department of Homeland Security with $215M, and NASA with $135M. The Department of the Interior obligated $26.4M, and other agencies listed include the Department of Justice at $5M and the Department of Commerce at $1.1M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does CACI Federal sell to the government?",
      "a": "CACI Federal sells primarily Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $1.1B in obligations and Engineering Services accounted for $648M. Other sizable markets include Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $258M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $231M."
